PATIENT EDUCATION

Treatment Explanation: The complete lack of estrogen is causing your brain's temperature control center to misfire constantly, triggering the severe sweats and the rapid heart rate (palpitations). The severe lack of sleep has driven your nervous system into a state of panic. The medications provided tonight will specifically calm the temperature center and force your brain to sleep, breaking the crisis cycle.
Actionable Steps: Take the sleeping tablet 30 minutes before bed tonight. Use the frozen gel pack technique for any breakthrough flashes, and ensure you see your regular GP next week to discuss estrogen replacement.

